it is still horrible (the source, I mean).  I would personally take a GREAT
PLEASURE shooting those people <grin> who came up with those OBSCURE
variable/function names, and who follow an OBSCURE standard of coding with
EXCESSIVE OVERmodularity in the source (TONS of .h and .c files), and just
plain messy (yuck).

On the other hand...NetHack exists...it RUNS...it's fun...it's been PORTED...
and I can continue, but I digress.  All this is definitely not the result of
a great coding standard, but a result of some smart and TWISTED minds,
hopelessly addicted, HACKING on the stuff, breathing it, etc.! :-)
(incidentally, the same can be said about MUD code, which is really infamous
for this).  BTW, Umoria's code is pretty NICE in my opinion (ie, I have found
it is very easy to read), but Umoria is soo boooring and looong, and it has not
items comparing to NetHack, etc...  Omega's code is not great, nor is it as bad
as NetHack's, but Omega is fun, it lack NetHack's arcade feeling (which I
happen to like), but it is SOOO much more ADVENTURE, and exploration, then
NetHack which is REALLY nice, and exactly THAT made NetHack seem boring and
FLAT, UNIdimensional...kill, gain experience, get items, next level, repeat
with any luck until success, and not much interesting will you learn...no
setting.  Gnomish mines and special levels are definitely an improvement in
that direction, but NetHack still has a long way to go...  On the other hand,
you can play nethack forever, but I doubt you will want to play Omega after you
finish it.

